# Milestone: v0.10.2
# Covers: legacy F3 — bare-prefix tag label `tag: stmt` parses without braces.
#         parse_tag_prefix previously required `{ ... }` after `:`.
#         This fixture confirms the bare-statement form is syntactically accepted
#         and the body executes (using integer as tag key, no Tag.new required).
#
# W5/v0.10.2: parse_tag_prefix now peeks at the next token; if LBRACE, calls
#         parse_block (existing behaviour); otherwise parses a single statement
#         and wraps it in an implicit single-statement AST_BLOCK so the emit
#         path is unchanged.  Closes legacy audit F3.
#
# See also: tests/chk/reactive/every/cancel_tag.chk (every() inside brace form —
#           can be updated to bare form now that this gap is closed).

var x = 0; var t = 0; t: x = 42; x
[00000000] 42
